What is CGHex
=============

CGHex allows the user to load data from any file, view and edit it in either
hex or ascii. A must for anyone playing games that use non-ascii format for
saving.

CGHex is a fork of GHex 1.2.1, ported from GNOME 1 to plain GTK 1.2. It is
renamed because GHex is still an active project.


Building
========

See the README at the top of cgtools.


Use
===

  cghex [FILE...]


Authors
=======

GHex was written by Jaka Mocnik <jaka.mocnik@kiss.uni-lj.si>, with
Chema Celorio <chema@celorio.com>.
